cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pldsc, please cite the software plus the method references below; the full method landscape (Popcorn, S-LDXR, MAMA, cov-LDSC and the 2026 meta-LDSC preprint) is maintained in docs/STRATEGY.md §5 and docs/PRIOR_ART.md."
title: "pldsc: population-aware LD Score regression research tools"
abstract: >-
  Research tools for LD Score regression when GWAS samples contain
  population structure. The live direction studies LDSC on multi-ancestry
  data: the LD score a fixed-effect meta-analysis actually follows (MA2),
  the factor kappa by which a single-ancestry LD score biases its h2
  (MA6, kappa = 0.75 for 75% EUR + 25% AFR at rho = 0.8 on 1000G chr22),
  and the corrections. Includes the archived estimator line's tested
  machinery (the mixed-model residual-precision operator P_c, the
  LD-score decomposition, the effective pair-df correction) and its
  negative-results record.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vilhjálmsson"
    given-names: "Bjarni Jóhann"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bvilhjal/PLDSC"
